WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:05.410
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, since Arrow
is on break this week I wanted to do a new

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.910
bonus Flash video.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.170
So this is going to be my Top 5 Flash Villains.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.940
We also got a good look at Grant Gustin in
the full costume.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.740
So we should probably talk about that first.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.250
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Arrow and Flash videos every week along

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.759
with bonus Q&amp;A videos.

00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:23.689
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.689
There’s still several episodes left in season
2 of Arrow and they’ll be filming the Flash

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:29.099
pilot for a couple more weeks.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:32.439
So first let’s talk about Grant Gustin’s
Flash costume.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.820
As expected it looks more like a tech suit
than straight up fabric like Stephen Amell’s

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.899
Arrow suit.

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.120
The same person made both of them.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.519
The pictures we’ve seen from the set don’t
include any special effects.

00:00:43.519 --> 00:00:48.070
But I think once they edit the footage they’ll
tweak the colors and highlights a little bit.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.620
If you remember when they debuted Stephen
Amell’s costume, it was a much more muted

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.239
green color than the bright version in the
comic books.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.219
They turned the color way down mostly for
practical reasons.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:00:59.340
One, it’s supposed to help hide his identity.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.739
Two, it can’t be too distracting on camera.

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:04.800
And three, bright colors look a little silly
in real life.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.009
They even muted the blue and red of Superman’s
costume in Man of Steel.

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:12.729
So that’s why the red we’re seeing is
so dark compared to the comic book version.

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:16.159
I think it looks pretty cool, I’m glad they
didn’t go crazy with the yellow lightning

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:17.159
bolt hilights.

00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:19.500
It would have been way too distracting.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.640
Their goal is to draw as much attention to
Grant Gustin’s face for viewers like you

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.830
and me, while at the same hiding his identity
from the other characters.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:32.090
Just like you’re always looking at Stephen
Amell’s face on screen, but Detective Lance

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.869
never questions his identity.

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:37.930
Here’s a quick history of the different
comic book versions of the Flash Suit starting

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.430
with Jay Garrick who may or may not be John
Wesley Shipp in the pilot.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:46.060
Jay Garrick’s costume has largely remained
unchanged over the years.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.780
When DC Rebooted everything with New 52 they
rebooted Jay Garrick in the Earth 2 series

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.579
with this alternate costume.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.820
So currently, this is what he looks like.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.950
But if he does appear in the pilot it’s
possible that they’ll stick with the golden

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.640
age version of his costume.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.820
Barry Allen’s costume has also largely stayed
the same since the debut of the character.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.700
During New 52 they did add some more texture
to the flash symbol on his chest though.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.470
As you can see, Grant Gustin’s version is
much less spandexy looking.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.810
Which is a good thing.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.500
We don’t know where he’ll get the costume
yet.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.690
Either from the ring or if it will be like
Stephen Amell’s costume and he’ll physically

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.980
have to climb into it like a regular pair
of pants.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.860
This is the Wally West costume, it like the
others has pretty much been the same forever.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.620
The big difference from the Barry Allen costume
is that the nose is covered.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.810
The New 52 version of Wally West, the current
version is actually debuting finally in Flash

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.580
Annual #3 April 30th.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.070
So he’ll finally be reintroduced to the
DC Universe just like all the other characters

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.750
after Flashpoint.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.060
This is what the brand new version of the
costume will look like.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.450
Imagine it in red though.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.380
This is just a variant.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:57.390
Be sure to let me know what you think of Grant
Gustin’s costume in the comments and how

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.650
you think he’s going to get it.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.090
And now let’s talk some villains.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:05.340
They’ve already announced the antagonists
of the pilot The Reverse Flash Edward Thawne

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.840
and Killer Frost played by Danielle Panabaker.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.030
But if everything goes according to plan there’s
going to be 23 episodes in season 1 just like

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.030
Arrow.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.220
So they’re going to need to pull in some
more villains from the comics.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:25.410
Remember Barry Allen and enemy Edward Thawne
work at a Police Station, so it’s entirely

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.250
likely that they’ll be hunting down and
arresting villains every week.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.250
Here are my top 5 that we need to see in season
1.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.250
Remember this is just season 1, so nothing
too crazy like Gorilla Grodd.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.540
Here we go, Number 5 - Heat Wave.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.480
Like some of my other picks he’s one of
the core Rogue’s.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.590
The most frequent recurring group of villains
the Flash runs into.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:42.200
Heat Wave as a child became obsessed with
fire and is essentially a pyromaniac, the

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.480
other Rogues like Captain Cold inspired him
to channel his obsession into a new identity,

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.870
which is when he took on the Heat Wave persona.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.780
Post-New 52 he was disfigured when he and
all the other Rogue’s gained their superpowers.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.860
Now he can generate fire naturally from his
body.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.420
It’s likely that on the show if they use
the character, that they’ll use the particle

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.710
accelerator explosion to give all the Rogues,
including Heat Wave, their metahuman abilities.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:07.870
But it’s also possible that they could do
it old school and have him use heat guns like

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.510
during Flash Rebirth.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:12.740
They did imply that we would be seeing more
super powered people on the Flash, but they

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:15.900
didn’t say how many or if everyone would
just have powers at the beginning of the show

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.010
or if people would develop them over time.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.109
Number 4 - The Axel Walker Trixter.

00:04:20.109 --> 00:04:23.030
He’s the current version of the character
in the comics.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.380
He was a normal person that took the name
from the original Trixter after he died.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.180
Right now in the comics he’s already had
his arm torn off by Gorilla Grodd and is kind

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.969
of exiled from the Rogues.

00:04:32.969 --> 00:04:36.979
He doesn’t have any superpowers, and is
really more of a nuisance to The Flash.

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:40.680
Think exploding yo-yo’s, he does have a
pair of shoes that allow him to fly for periods

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.680
of time.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.020
I can only imagine how the tv show would deal
with that.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:49.850
Number 3 - Weather Wizard like the other Rogues
also gained superpowers during the New 52

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:50.850
Reboot.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:54.590
The name explains everything, but because
of the way his powers work, the more he uses

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.599
them to control weather, the more depressed
he gets.

00:04:57.599 --> 00:04:59.050
Which is kind of funny.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:03.330
As part of the comics reboot, he goes after
Dr Elias, who the Rogues blame for the accident

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.289
that gave them superpowers.

00:05:05.289 --> 00:05:10.210
The tv show is substituting the character
Tom Cavanagh is playing Harrison Wells for

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.530
the Dr Elias character in the comics.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:17.120
Harrison Wells is the person who is blamed
for the particle accelerator explosion.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.150
So the rogues on the show will probably try
to get revenge on him at some point and Grant

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.430
Gustin will have to stop them.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.340
Number 2 - Captain Cold.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:28.169
One of the interesting things about the character
is that even though he is a supervillain,

00:05:28.169 --> 00:05:29.740
he still has a moral code.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.580
He’s the one usually quoting the phrase,
“Rule Number 1 of the Rogues.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.039
You Never Kill A Flash.”

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:39.099
He does have a sister that he cares about
so of all the second tier Flash villains,

00:05:39.099 --> 00:05:41.840
he’s the most complex.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.979
There can be no Flash show without Captain
Cold, so of all the people on my list, he’s

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:48.009
the most likely we’ll see during season
1.

00:05:48.009 --> 00:05:49.009
But he’s a pretty big deal, so I don’t
expect him to appear until later in season

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:50.009
1.

00:05:50.009 --> 00:05:52.069
During the new 52 comics he ended up working
with and double crossing the Flash.

00:05:52.069 --> 00:05:58.479
So on the show he could team up with Grant
Gustin the same way Oliver and Diggle are

00:05:58.479 --> 00:06:00.029
teaming up with the Suicide Squad.

00:06:00.029 --> 00:06:03.719
and my number 1 villain I want to see in season
1.

00:06:03.719 --> 00:06:04.719
The Black Flash.

00:06:04.719 --> 00:06:08.449
He’s the physical embodiment of death, so
even though he’s a character.

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:10.810
He’s really more of an abstract idea.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.389
In the comics, the most recent version of
the character is just a negative aspect of

00:06:14.389 --> 00:06:15.389
the speed force.

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:17.469
During rebirth Barry Allen was possessed by
the Black Flash and started killing other

00:06:17.469 --> 00:06:18.469
people connected to the speed force.

00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:19.849
So essentially it’s like balancing the scales
on a physics level.

00:06:19.849 --> 00:06:23.599
There’s a positive aspect of the speed force
that Barry Allen and all the other Flashes

00:06:23.599 --> 00:06:25.840
get their power from, including Professor
Zoom.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.009
And then there’s the negative aspect of
the Speed Force, which the Black Flash draws

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:31.310
power from.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:34.719
As you saw earlier in the video, they’re
bringing Wally West back in the comics next

00:06:34.719 --> 00:06:37.539
month and he looks like a version of the Black
Flash.

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:40.139
So I’m sure the story will have something
to do with that.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:44.259
So now it’s your turn, let me know which
of the Rogues or other Flash villains do you

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:46.249
want to see on the show in season 1.

00:06:46.249 --> 00:06:48.229
Remember, the crazier villains like Gorilla
Grodd probably won’t come first.

00:06:48.229 --> 00:06:50.779
Just like on Arrow, they’ll probably use
the lesser villains first.

00:06:50.779 --> 00:06:51.999
Which means the Rogues.

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:55.069
Next week Arrow is back and it’s the Suicide
Squad episode, be sure to subscribe to get

00:06:55.069 --> 00:06:56.069
my video.

00:06:56.069 --> 00:06:58.909
We’re going to see Harley Quinn for the
first time.

00:06:58.909 --> 00:07:01.719
She’s being played by Caitlin Alexa.

00:07:01.719 --> 00:07:06.039
You can learn all about that in my last Arrow
video by clicking here and you can click here

00:07:06.039 --> 00:07:08.379
to learn more about season 1 of The Flash.

00:07:08.379 --> 00:07:09.949
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:10.400
High Fives!

